# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. These are READ AT BUILD TIME.
#
# Supabase cross-device sync (optional). Leave blank to run fully local-only —
# the app still works; the Sync section in Settings just shows "not configured".
# The anon key is a PUBLIC client key and is safe to ship in a frontend build,
# because Row Level Security (see supabase/schema.sql) restricts every row to
# its owning user. Never put the Supabase *service_role* key here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Self-hosted quote proxy (recommended — see proxy/cloudflare-worker.js and
# SECURITY.md). A URL prefix ending in `?url=`, which the app appends the
# encoded Yahoo URL to. When set it is used ALONE: the public proxy chain in
# src/lib/proxies.ts is skipped entirely and the build narrows the Content
# Security Policy down to your worker's origin.
# VITE_QUOTES_PROXY=https://money-monitor-quotes.<you>.workers.dev/?url=

# Only needed for a GitHub Pages *project* site (username.github.io/<repo>/).
# The CI workflow sets this automatically; for a local production build of a
# project site you can set it yourself, e.g. VITE_BASE=/finance-app/
# VITE_BASE=/
